{
 "title": "Regex in Python: Cheat Sheet",
 "description": "A one-page reference for Python's re module, with an example computed by Python for every row. Use the step-by-step guide to learn it, the playground to try it.",
 "sections": [
  {
   "name": "Characters and classes",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Pattern",
      "Matches",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`abc`",
       "the literal text",
       "`abc` on `xabcx` gives `['abc']`"
      ],
      [
       "`.`",
       "any character except newline",
       "`c.t` on `cat c-t ct` gives `['cat', 'c-t']`"
      ],
      [
       "`[abc]`",
       "one of a, b, c",
       "`[abc]` on `cabbage` gives `['c', 'a', 'b', 'b', 'a']`"
      ],
      [
       "`[a-z]`",
       "a range",
       "`[a-c]` on `abcdef` gives `['a', 'b', 'c']`"
      ],
      [
       "`[^abc]`",
       "anything but a, b, c",
       "`[^abc]` on `abcxyz` gives `['x', 'y', 'z']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\d` `\\D`",
       "digit / non-digit",
       "`\\d` on `a1b2` gives `['1', '2']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\w` `\\W`",
       "word char / non-word char",
       "`\\w+` on `hi there!` gives `['hi', 'there']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\s` `\\S`",
       "whitespace / non-whitespace",
       "`\\S+` on `a  b c` gives `['a', 'b', 'c']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\.` `\\\\` `\\(`",
       "a literal special character",
       "`\\.` on `a.b.c` gives `['.', '.']`"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Quantifiers",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Pattern",
      "Meaning",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`x*`",
       "0 or more",
       "`ab*` on `a ab abb` gives `['a', 'ab', 'abb']`"
      ],
      [
       "`x+`",
       "1 or more",
       "`\\d+` on `a1 b22` gives `['1', '22']`"
      ],
      [
       "`x?`",
       "0 or 1",
       "`colou?r` on `color colour` gives `['color', 'colour']`"
      ],
      [
       "`x{3}`",
       "exactly 3",
       "`\\d{3}` on `1234567` gives `['123', '456']`"
      ],
      [
       "`x{2,4}`",
       "2 to 4",
       "`\\d{2,4}` on `1 22 333 4444 55555` gives `['22', '333', '4444', '5555']`"
      ],
      [
       "`x*?` `x+?` `x??`",
       "lazy: as few as possible",
       "`<.+?>` on `<a><b>` gives `['<a>', '<b>']`"
      ],
      [
       "`x+` (greedy)",
       "as many as possible",
       "`<.+>` on `<a><b>` gives `['<a><b>']`"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Anchors and boundaries",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Pattern",
      "Meaning",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`^`",
       "start of string (line with `re.M`)",
       "`^\\w+` on `one two` gives `['one']`"
      ],
      [
       "`$`",
       "end of string (or before a final newline)",
       "`\\w+$` on `one two` gives `['two']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\A` `\\Z`",
       "very start / very end",
       "`\\Aone` on `one one` gives `['one']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\b`",
       "word boundary",
       "`\\bcat\\b` on `cat concat cat` gives `['cat', 'cat']`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\B`",
       "not a word boundary",
       "`\\Bcat` on `cat concat` gives `['cat']`"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Groups and alternation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Pattern",
      "Meaning",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`a|b`",
       "a or b",
       "`cat|dog` on `a cat, a dog` gives `['cat', 'dog']`"
      ],
      [
       "`(...)`",
       "capturing group",
       "`(\\d+)-(\\d+)` on `10-20` gives `[('10', '20')]`"
      ],
      [
       "`(?:...)`",
       "grouping only, no capture",
       "`(?:ab)+` on `ababab` gives `['ababab']`"
      ],
      [
       "`(?P<n>...)`",
       "named group",
       "`m.group('n')`, `m.groupdict()`"
      ],
      [
       "`\\1`",
       "repeat group 1's text",
       "`(\\w)\\1` on `hello bookkeeper` gives `['l', 'o', 'k', 'e']`"
      ],
      [
       "`(?P=n)`",
       "repeat named group n's text",
       "`(?P<c>\\w)(?P=c)` is the same as `(\\w)\\1`"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Lookaround",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Pattern",
      "Passes when",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`(?=x)`",
       "x is next",
       "`\\w+(?=!)` on `hi! yo` gives `['hi']`"
      ],
      [
       "`(?!x)`",
       "x is not next",
       "`\\d+(?!\\d|px)` on `10px 20em` gives `['20']`"
      ],
      [
       "`(?<=x)`",
       "x is just before",
       "`(?<=\\$)\\d+` on `$5 and 6` gives `['5']`"
      ],
      [
       "`(?<!x)`",
       "x is not just before",
       "`(?<!\\$)\\b\\d+` on `$5 and 6` gives `['6']`"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Flags",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Flag",
      "Inline",
      "Effect"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`re.I`",
       "`(?i)`",
       "ignore case"
      ],
      [
       "`re.M`",
       "`(?m)`",
       "`^` `$` at each line"
      ],
      [
       "`re.S`",
       "`(?s)`",
       "`.` matches newline"
      ],
      [
       "`re.X`",
       "`(?x)`",
       "verbose: spaces ignored, `#` comments"
      ],
      [
       "`re.A`",
       "`(?a)`",
       "ASCII-only `\\w` `\\d` `\\s` `\\b`"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "Combine with `|`: `re.compile(r\"...\", re.I | re.M)`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Functions",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Call",
      "Returns"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`re.search(p, s)`",
       "first match anywhere, or `None`"
      ],
      [
       "`re.match(p, s)`",
       "match at the start, or `None`"
      ],
      [
       "`re.fullmatch(p, s)`",
       "match of the whole string, or `None`"
      ],
      [
       "`re.findall(p, s)`",
       "list of matches (the groups, if the pattern has any)"
      ],
      [
       "`re.finditer(p, s)`",
       "iterator of match objects"
      ],
      [
       "`re.sub(p, repl, s)`",
       "string with matches replaced (`\\1`, `\\g<name>`, or a function)"
      ],
      [
       "`re.split(p, s)`",
       "list of the pieces between matches"
      ],
      [
       "`re.compile(p, flags)`",
       "reusable pattern object"
      ],
      [
       "`re.escape(s)`",
       "s with special characters escaped"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "Match object",
      "Gives"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "`m.group()`",
       "whole match"
      ],
      [
       "`m.group(1)` `m.group('n')`",
       "one group"
      ],
      [
       "`m.groups()`",
       "all groups"
      ],
      [
       "`m.groupdict()`",
       "named groups as a dict"
      ],
      [
       "`m.span()` `m.start()` `m.end()`",
       "position"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Ready-made patterns (shape checks, use with re.fullmatch)",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "headers": [
      "For",
      "Pattern"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Digits only",
       "`\\d+`"
      ],
      [
       "Hex colour",
       "`#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}`"
      ],
      [
       "US ZIP, +4 optional",
       "`\\d{5}(?:-\\d{4})?`"
      ],
      [
       "Time 24h",
       "`(?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d`"
      ],
      [
       "Date YYYY-MM-DD",
       "`\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])`"
      ],
      [
       "IPv4",
       "`(?:(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d\\d|[1-9]?\\d)\\.){3}(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d\\d|[1-9]?\\d)`"
      ],
      [
       "Simple email",
       "`[\\w.+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)+`"
      ],
      [
       "Collapse whitespace",
       "`re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s)`"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Common mistakes",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "list",
     "items": [
      "**Forgetting the r:** write `r\"\\d+\"`, not `\"\\d+\"`.",
      "**search when you meant fullmatch:** `re.search(r\"\\d{3}\", \"a123b\")` is a match. To validate a whole value use `re.fullmatch`.",
      "**Unescaped dot:** `3.14` also matches `3x14`. Write `3\\.14`.",
      "**Greedy `.*`:** it runs to the last possible match. Use `.*?` or a negated class such as `[^\"]*`.",
      "**findall with groups:** it returns the groups, not the whole match. Use `(?:...)` or `finditer`.",
      "**`|` without a group:** `^cat|dog$` is not the whole-string check you meant. Write `^(?:cat|dog)$`.",
      "**`[a-Z]`:** ranges go by character code and this one is an error. Write `[a-zA-Z]`.",
      "**`[abc|def]`:** inside brackets `|` is a literal character. Use `(?:abc|def)`.",
      "**Nested quantifiers:** `(a+)+` can hang on a failing match.",
      "**Parsing HTML or JSON with a regex:** use a real parser."
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
